## output.soar -- agent-world: 5 elaborations.
## v2.47: the output map (World-Conventions L10-002, L10-014). The top state's ^output-map says how a task operator's
## action is written to the output-link and which ^status values the environment reports. An environment declares its
## own map as ^environment-output-map on the top state; without one, the default map below applies. The default is the
## ^perform-action form (Thor-Soar's, World-Conventions L20-042), which the test harnesses complete, so agents that
## declare nothing run as before v2.47.
## Map fields: ^command <attr> and ^name-attribute <attr> (the command is (<ol> ^<command> <c>) (<c> ^<name-attribute>
## <action-handle>)), or ^command-is-action-handle true (the command is (<ol> ^<action-handle> <c>)); ^argument1 to
## ^argument3 <attr> (the attribute each operator argument is written under); ^done-status (removed from the
## output-link), ^success-status (an executed-action event), ^error-status (a failed-action event; kept on the
## output-link and its ^error-info logged); optional ^action <a> entries with ^action-handle <h> and their own command
## and argument fields for single actions; ^rules environment when the environment's own rules write the commands.

## Elaborate top-state output-map: the environment's map.
sp {agent-world*elaborate*top-state*output-map*environment
   :default
   (state <s> ^superstate nil
              ^environment-output-map <m>)
-->
   (<s> ^output-map <m>)
}

## Elaborate top-state output-map: the default map (the ^perform-action form) when the environment declares none.
sp {agent-world*elaborate*top-state*output-map*default
   :default
   (state <s> ^superstate nil
             -^environment-output-map)
-->
   (<s> ^output-map <m>)
   (<m> ^command perform-action
        ^name-attribute name
        ^argument1 argument1
        ^argument2 argument2
        ^argument3 argument3
        ^done-status interrupted complete success
        ^success-status success
        ^error-status error failure)
}

## Elaborate output-link remove-command: remove a command once its status is one of the map's done statuses.
sp {agent-world*elaborate*output-link*remove-command
   :default
   :o-support
   (state <s> ^superstate nil
              ^output-map.done-status <status>
              ^io.output-link <ol>)
   (<ol> ^<command> <value>)
   (<value> ^status <status>)
-->
   (<ol> ^<command> <value> -)
}

## Elaborate top-state any remove completed agent-event -> removes the agent-event.
## Apply Rule for any top-state operator:
## If an agent-event on the output-link is marked complete,
sp {agent-world*elaborate*top-state*any*remove*completed*agent-event
   :default
   :o-support
   (state <s> ^superstate nil
              ^io.output-link <out>)
   (<out> ^agent-event <event>)
   (<event> ^status complete)
-->
   (<out> ^agent-event <event> -)
}

## Elaborate output-link error: log the ^error-info of a command whose status is one of the map's error statuses.
sp {agent-world*elaborate*output-link*error
   :default
   :o-support
   (state <s> ^superstate nil
              ^output-map.error-status <status>
              ^io.output-link <ol>)
   (<ol> ^<command> <perform-action>)
   (<perform-action> ^status <status>
                     ^error-info <string>)
-->
   (log 1 (crlf) |Output Error: | <string>)
}
